This game here is meant as a recreation of an old mobile game called Jumpstun.

## Building

Requires CMake (3.11+) and a C compiler. raylib is downloaded automatically during configuration.

    cmake . -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5
    make
    ./spiel

Alternatively, `run.sh` cleans previous build files, rebuilds and starts the game.

## Controls

- Desktop: X / Space / click to jump, arrow keys + X in menus, BACKSPACE to go back
- Android: tap to jump and to use the menus, the back button goes back

## Android

The Android app lives in `android/` and shares the game code in `src/`.
Requires JDK 17+ and the Android SDK with `platforms;android-36`, `build-tools;36.0.0`,
`ndk;29.0.14206865` and `cmake;3.31.6`.

    cd android
    echo "sdk.dir=$HOME/Android/Sdk" > local.properties
    ./gradlew assembleDebug
    adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk

The APK ends up in `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/`. GitHub Actions also builds it on every push.

### Ads (Google AdMob)

The game offers optional rewarded videos: +10 coins in the shop and one revive per run.
A GDPR consent dialog (Google UMP) is shown where required, and a PRIVACY button in the
menu lets players change their choice.

Debug builds always use Google's test ads. For a release with real ads:

1. Create an app and a rewarded ad unit in AdMob and set up the GDPR message under
   "Privacy & messaging".
2. Put the IDs and your signing key into `~/.gradle/gradle.properties` (never commit them):

        jumperchicken.admobAppId=ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX~YYYYYYYYYY
        jumperchicken.admobRewardedId=ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/ZZZZZZZZZZ
        jumperchicken.keystore=/path/to/release.jks
        jumperchicken.keystorePassword=...
        jumperchicken.keyAlias=...
        jumperchicken.keyPassword=...

3. Build with `./gradlew bundleRelease` and upload the `.aab` to the Google Play Console.

Never tap your own real ads; AdMob bans accounts for that. Use the debug build for testing.
